*(≈ 8 hours, walk‑friendly, all major sights covered – includes a ticket‑option you can book instantly)*  

Below is a ready‑to‑copy itinerary that strings together the city’s most‑visited attractions, plus the price‑and‑cancellation details for the **“Admission to the Acropolis and the Parthenon”** ticket that the API returned for you.  An optional half‑day extension to **Cape Sounion** (Temple of Poseidon) is also included.

---

### 📅 Full‑Day Itinerary (Mon‑Fri, Saturday‑Sunday works the same)

| Time (local) | Stop | What to See / Do | Practical Details |
|--------------|------|------------------|-------------------|
| **08:30 – 09:00** | **Monastiraki Metro Station** (Line 1 / 3) | Grab a coffee & a pastry at a nearby café (e.g., **Mokka**). | Metro ticket ≈ €1.20 (single ride). |
| **09:00 – 11:30** | **Acropolis & Parthenon** | • Walk the marble steps up to the **Parthenon** (dedicated to Athena).<br>• Visit the **Erechtheion** (Caryatids), **Propylaea**, and **Temple of Athena Nike**.<br>• Panoramic city‑and‑sea view. | **Ticket (API product)** – “Admission to the Acropolis and the Parthenon”<br>• **Price:** US $14.08 ≈ €13 (price shown in USD; conversion at the time of purchase).<br>• **Cancellation:** *No free cancellation* (the API flagged `hasFreeCancellation: false`).<br>• **Opening:** 08:00‑20:00 (Apr‑Oct) / 08:00‑17:00 (Nov‑Mar).<br>• **Suggested stay:** 2 h 30 m. |
| **11:30 – 12:30** | **Acropolis Museum** (optional) | • Original marble sculptures (Caryatids, Parthenon frieze).<br>• Top‑floor “Parthenon Hall” with a perfect view of the Acropolis. | **Opening:** 08:00‑20:00 (Apr‑Oct) / 08:00‑17:00 (Nov‑Mar).<br>**Ticket:** €10 (adult) – free with the combined Acropolis ticket.<br>**Stay:** ~1 h. |
| **12:30 – 13:30** | **Plaka (old town)** | • Wander the narrow, cobblestone lanes, browse souvenir shops, and snap photos in **Anafiotika** (a tiny “village‑in‑the‑city”). | No entry fee. |
| **13:30 – 14:30** | **Lunch in Plaka** | Try classic Greek dishes – **Moussaka**, **Souvlaki**, **Greek salad**, **Baklava**. Recommended tavernas: **Yiasemi**, **Kuzina**, **Taverna Saita**. | Expect €12‑€20 per person. |
| **14:30 – 16:30** | **National Archaeological Museum** | • Greece’s largest collection: **Mask of Agamemnon**, **Antikythera mechanism**, golden funerary masks, **Statue of Poseidon**.<br>• Great indoor alternative if the weather is hot. | **Opening:** 08:00‑20:00 (Apr‑Oct) / 08:00‑17:00 (Nov‑Mar).<br>**Ticket:** €10 (adult).<br>**Stay:** 2 h. |
| **16:30 – 17:30** | **Syntagma Square – Changing of the Guard** | • Watch the ceremonial guard change at the **Hellenic Parliament** (every hour on the hour).<br>• Photo with the **Eternal Flame** monument. | Free. |
| **17:30 – 19:00** | **Lycabettus Hill (Teleferik)** | • Take the **cable car** from **Kolonaki** (or hike up if you prefer).<br>• Sunset panorama over the Acropolis, the sea, and the whole city. | **Cable‑car ticket:** €7 round‑trip (optional – free if you hike).<br>**Opening:** 09:00‑22:00 (seasonal). |
| **19:00 – 20:30** | **Dinner in Kolonaki** | Upscale dining with a view – **Strofi**, **Mavro Provato**, or **Papadakis** (seafood). | Expect €20‑€35 per person. |
| **20:30 +** | **Optional Nightlife** | Head to **Gazi** for bars & live music, or a rooftop cocktail at **360 ° Bar** in Monastiraki. | No extra cost beyond drinks. |

#### **Cost Summary (per adult)**  

| Item | Approx. Price |
|------|---------------|
| Acropolis ticket (API product) | €13 (≈ US $14.08) |
| Acropolis Museum (included) | €0 |
| National Archaeological Museum | €10 |
| Lycabettus Hill cable‑car | €7 |
| Meals (lunch + dinner) | €30‑€55 |
| Misc. (coffee, snacks, metro) | €5‑€10 |
| **Total** | **≈ €72‑€92** |

> **Note:** The Acropolis ticket shown above has **no free cancellation** (as indicated by the API). If you need a refundable option, you can book a “skip‑the‑line” version from the same provider – it usually costs a few euros more but offers free cancellation up to 24 h before the visit.

---

## 🌅 Optional Half‑Day Extension – **Cape Sounion & Temple of Poseidon**

A classic “Athens sunset” day‑trip to the southern tip of the Attica peninsula.  The API already gave you a concise description of the temple:

*“A 5th‑century BC marble temple perched on a cliff 60 m above the Aegean Sea, dedicated to the god of the sea. The site offers dramatic sea‑views, especially at sunset, and a small on‑site museum displaying finds from the sanctuary.”*

| Time | Activity | Details |
|------|----------|---------|
| **08:00 – 09:00** | Depart from **Kifissos Bus Terminal** (or book a guided tour) | **KTEL** bus A8 to Sounion – €4.50 one‑way, ~1 h 30 m ride. |
| **10:30 – 12:30** | **Temple of Poseidon (Sounion)** | • Explore the marble ruins and the tiny museum.<br>**Opening:** 08:00‑20:00 (summer) / 08:00‑17:00 (winter).<br>**Ticket:** €8 (adult). |
| **12:30 – 13:30** | Lunch at **Sounion Bay** (sea‑view tavern) | Fresh fish, Greek salad, ouzo. |
| **13:30 – 15:00** | **Relax on the beach** or **visit the lighthouse** | Optional swim or short hike for extra sea‑views. |
| **15:00 – 16:30** | Return to Athens | Same bus route, or a private transfer (≈ €30‑€40). |

**Extra cost:** ≈ €30‑€45 (transport + entry + lunch).

---

## 📌 Quick Practical Tips for the Whole Day

| Topic | Advice |
|-------|--------|
| **Best travel months** | Late spring (April‑June) or early autumn (Sept‑Oct) – pleasant weather, fewer crowds. |
| **Getting around** | Athens Metro (Lines 1, 2, 3) covers most sites. A 24‑hour ticket costs €4.10 for unlimited rides. |
| **Footwear** | Comfortable walking shoes – the Acropolis steps are steep and uneven. |
| **Sun protection** | Hat, sunscreen, and a water bottle – especially in summer. |
| **Language** | English is widely spoken; a few Greek phrases (“Kalimera” – good morning, “Efharisto” – thank you) are appreciated. |
| **Cash vs. Card** | Most restaurants and museums accept cards; small tavernas or street vendors may prefer cash (euros). |
| **Safety** | Athens is generally safe; keep an eye on belongings in crowded areas (e.g., Monastiraki market). |

---

### 🎉 Ready to explore?

1. **Book the Acropolis ticket** (the API product “Admission to the Acropolis and the Parthenon”) – you can do it instantly through the provider’s website or the travel‑booking platform you’re using.  
2. **Copy the schedule** into your travel planner, adjust the start time to match your arrival, and you’ll have a seamless, culturally rich day discovering the heart of Athens.  

If you’d like a **food‑focused walking tour**, a **private guide**, or **night‑time visits** (e.g., the Acropolis illuminated after dark), just let me know and I can tailor the plan further!

